.TH "YAMLR-AUDIT" "1" "March 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBDeep Compliance Audit (Alias for [scan](yamlr_scan.md))\fR
.PP
The \fBaudit\fR command is an alias for \fByamlr scan\fR. It is provided for users who prefer a compliance-focused terminology.
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
yamlr audit [PATH]... [FLAGS]
.RE
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Performs the same deep semantic auditing as \fByamlr scan\fR, including:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Syntax & Structure Validation**
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Kubernetes Schema Checks**
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **OPA Policy Enforcement**
For a full list of features, flags, and examples, please refer to the [yamlr scan](yamlr_scan.md) manual.
.PP
.SH "🔬 SCIENTIFIC MODE (BENCHMARKING)"
The \fBaudit\fR command includes a specialized \fBScientific Mode\fR for benchmarking the healing engine against a known-good corpus.
.PP
.nf
.RS
# Run a full benchmark on a directory of manifests
yamlr audit ./tests/corpus --bench

# Summary-only for CI/CD metrics
yamlr audit ./tests/corpus --bench --summary-only

# View forensic surgical metrics and HAS scores directly
yamlr audit ./tests/corpus --bench --stats
.RE
.fi
.SS "Metrics Produced:"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **HAS (Healing Accuracy Score)**: The percentage of manifests successfully healed and validated against the K8s API (or internal oracle).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Detect Rate**: Percentage of manifests where issues were identified.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **FP Rate**: False Positive rate (aiming for 0.0%).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Reconstruction Depth**: Classification of repairs as **Light** (Metadata/Indentation), **Medium** (Value coercion), or **Heavy** (Structural/Epistemic).
.SH "🛡 UNIVERSAL EXPERT FLAGS & OPTIONS"
These flags are available across almost all primary Yamlr commands, including \fBaudit\fR:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--output FORMAT\fR**: Report format (text, json, sarif).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--opa-bundle <PATH>\fR**: Path or URL to OPA bundle.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--kyverno-report <PATH>\fR**: Path to ingest a Kyverno \fBPolicyReport\fR JSON file.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--diff\fR**: Show visual diff of changes (Preview mode).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--dry-run\fR**: Alias for \fB--diff\fR.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--fast\fR**: Skip heavy semantic analysis for maximum speed.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--kube-version <V>\fR**: Force a specific Kubernetes version (e.g., \fB1.31\fR). Alias: **\fB--k8s-version <V>\fR**.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--max-depth <N>\fR**: Limit recursive scanning depth (Default: 10).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--ext <list>\fR**: Comma-separated list of file extensions (Default: \fB.yaml,.yml\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--concurrency <N>\fR**: Number of parallel worker processes.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--strict\fR**: Treat all schema warnings as hard errors.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--compact\fR**: Use minimal whitespace (2-space indent) in output.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--health-threshold <0-100>\fR**: Minimum score to pass (Default: 70).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--namespace <name>\fR**: Default namespace for generated resources.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--check-deprecations\fR**: Audit for and record deprecated K8s APIs.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--cpu-limit <limit>\fR**: Default CPU for auto-injection (e.g., \fB500m\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--mem-limit <limit>\fR**: Default Memory for auto-injection (e.g., \fB512Mi\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--enforce-limits\fR**: Auto-inject missing CPU/Memory limits.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--enforce-probes\fR**: Auto-inject missing Liveness/Readiness probes.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--enforce-namespace\fR**: Auto-inject default namespace if missing.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--fix-tags\fR**: Auto-remediate \fB:latest\fR or missing image tags.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--harden\fR**: Apply security hardening (Non-root, Read-only FS).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--stream-to <FILE>\fR**: Batch-mode: Stream results to NDJSON (prevents RAM saturation).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--fail-on <CHOICE>\fR**: Exit 1 if specified severity found (error/warning/any).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB-s\fR, \fB--summary-only\fR**: Show aggregate stats only (recommended for 100+ files).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB-p\fR, \fB--plain\fR**: ASCII-only output mode (Recommended for Log redirection).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--verbose\fR**: Show full audit logs and engine stages.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB-q\fR, \fB--quiet\fR**: Minimal output mode (CI/CD optimized; errors and exit codes only).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--identity-mode {infer,strict}\fR**: Control how Yamlr identifies resources (Default: infer).
